{% comment %}
  Oberndoerfer Milano - MOBILE MENU DRAWER (PART 9)
  -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Rendered from oberndoerfer-type-overrides.liquid.

  Mostly CSS. The ACCORDION at the foot of this file is the one piece of JS,
  written as progressive enhancement: if it never runs, the drawer simply
  renders fully expanded exactly as it did before, and every link still works.

  WHY THIS EXISTS
  PART 4 of the type-overrides snippet deliberately scoped the shared heading
  scale to `main`, which left the header, footer and MENU DRAWER on the theme's
  own type scale. Measured on the draft theme at 375x812 before this change:

    top-level items ("HOME", "COLLECTIONS")  28px uppercase, 47px row
    child items ("NEW IN", "BAGS", ...)      16px, but 114-140px rows (images)
    drawer width                             356px of a 375px viewport (95%)
    open transition                          transform .2s

  WHAT THIS SNIPPET DOES
  - Top-level 28px -> 16px uppercase, tracked, weight 500. It is a nav label,
    and at 28px it was louder than the mobile h1 (24px), inverting hierarchy.
  - Non-grid children 14px, muted, >=44px tap rows.
  - COLLECTION THUMBNAILS ARE SHOWN, in a 2-column grid, at one fixed crop.
  - Top-level items with a submenu are COLLAPSED BY DEFAULT and expand on tap.
  - Drawer fills the whole viewport on phones.
  - Open transition .2s -> .42s on a soft curve, with a reduced-motion opt-out.

  COLLECTION THUMBNAILS - OWNER DECISION, 2026-08-15
  An earlier revision HID these thumbnails on the argument that Hermes / The Row
  / Bottega Veneta / Miu Miu / Gucci all use pure typography in mobile nav. The
  owner has asked twice for the collection pictures back, so they are restored.
  That decision is settled - do not re-litigate it in a future pass.

  The two real defects behind the original complaint are fixed here rather than
  by removing the images:
  1. INCONSISTENT CROP. The source images have different intrinsic ratios
     (verified: 800x802, 800x533, ...), so cards in a row rendered at different
     heights and rows never lined up. One enforced `aspect-ratio` +
     `object-fit: cover` makes every thumbnail the same square. Display-only.
  2. LOW CONTRAST. Pale beige-on-beige shots bled into the white drawer. Fixed
     with a warm ground plus a hairline inset border.

  BUGFIX 2026-08-15 - LOCALIZATION SELECTOR OVERLAPPING THE GRID
  The previous revision set `min-height: 100%` on `.menu-drawer__navigation`.
  `.menu-drawer` is `display: flex; flex-direction: column` and the nav is
  `flex: 0 1 auto`, so that resolved the nav's box to exactly the drawer height
  (812px) while its actual content was 1624px. The nav's `overflow` is
  `visible`, so the menu content spilled straight out of its box, while the
  `.menu-drawer__utility-links` row - which holds the USD / EN region+language
  selector - was laid out at 856px, i.e. directly on top of the spilled
  collection grid. That is what put "USD / EN" over the Small Leather Goods
  thumbnail.
  FIX: no min-height. `flex: 1 0 auto` lets the nav grow to fill the drawer when
  the menu is short (keeping the utility row at the bottom) and take its natural
  height when the menu is tall, with `.menu-drawer` as the single scroll
  container. DO NOT reintroduce a percentage min-height on this element.

  FULL-SCREEN DRAWER - OWNER REQUEST, 2026-08-15
  The theme ships `.menu-drawer` as `position: fixed; inset: 0`, so it was
  already full-bleed geometrically, but height came from `100vh`, which ignores
  the mobile address bar and leaves a strip of page showing on real devices.
  Pinned to `100dvh` where supported, with `100vh` kept first as the fallback.
  NOTE: the previous revision also targeted `.menu-drawer__inner-container`,
  which DOES NOT EXIST in this theme - verified in the live DOM. The real inner
  element is `.menu-drawer__navigation`.

  ACCORDION - OWNER REQUEST, 2026-08-15
  Everything rendered expanded on open, so the first impression was a wall
  including nine collection images. Top-level items that have a submenu now
  start collapsed and expand on tap, one at a time (opening one closes the
  others), which keeps the drawer near one screen.

  Two details worth knowing before changing this:
  - The parent rows are REAL LINKS (/collections, /pages/about-us,
    /pages/personalization), so making them toggles would strand those
    destinations. "About us" and "Bespoke" already repeat themselves as their
    own first child, so they lose nothing. "Collections" does not, so a
    "View all" link is appended to its panel. The injection is conditional -
    it only happens when the parent's href is not already among its children.
  - preventDefault only fires when the mobile media query matches AND the
    script has run, so with JS unavailable the rows stay ordinary links.

  NOT DONE HERE (needs the P0.4 navigation decision first):
  the LABELS are still merchandising-led ("NEW IN", "FEATURED PRODUCTS",
  "COLLECTIONS") rather than customer-intent-led. Renaming them edits the
  Shopify navigation object and hits desktop too, so it belongs to the nav
  restructure, not to this pass.

  NOTE ON !important: this snippet is injected ahead of the theme stylesheet,
  so equal-specificity theme rules would otherwise win the cascade.
{% endcomment %}
{% style %}
  /* ---------- PART 9: mobile menu drawer ---------- */

  /* -- type: top level becomes a nav label, not a headline -- */
  .menu-drawer__menu-item--mainlist,
  .menu-drawer__menu-item--mainlist .menu-drawer__menu-item-text {
    font-size: 1rem !important;
    line-height: 1.35 !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.09em !important;
    font-weight: 500 !important;
    color: #18120C !important;
  }
  .menu-drawer__menu-item--mainlist {
    padding-block: 14px !important;
  }

  /* -- children (plain text lists): quieter, comfortable tap rows -- */
  .menu-drawer__menu--childlist {
    padding-inline-start: 2px !important;
    margin-block-start: 2px !important;
  }
  .menu-drawer__menu-item--child {
    display: flex !important;
    flex-direction: row !important;
    align-items: center !important;
    justify-content: flex-start !important;
    text-align: left !important;
    min-height: 44px !important;
    height: auto !important;
    padding-block: 4px !important;
    font-size: 0.875rem !important;
    line-height: 1.4 !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em !important;
    font-weight: 400 !important;
    color: rgba(24, 18, 12, 0.62) !important;
  }
  .menu-drawer__menu-item--child:hover,
  .menu-drawer__menu-item--child:focus-visible {
    color: #18120C !important;
  }

  /* -- COLLECTION THUMBNAIL GRID: restored, one consistent crop -- */
  .menu-drawer__menu--grid {
    display: grid !important;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)) !important;
    gap: 22px 12px !important;
    align-items: start !important;
    padding-inline: 2px 4px !important;
    margin-block: 12px 6px !important;
  }
  .menu-drawer__menu--grid .menu-drawer__list-item {
    min-width: 0 !important;
    border: 0 !important;
  }

  /* card: image stacked over its label, both flush left */
  .menu-drawer__menu--grid .menu-drawer__menu-item--child {
    display: flex !important;
    flex-direction: column !important;
    align-items: stretch !important;
    justify-content: flex-start !important;
    text-align: left !important;
    min-height: 0 !important;
    padding-block: 0 !important;
    font-size: 0.8125rem !important;
    line-height: 1.35 !important;
    letter-spacing: 0.07em !important;
    font-weight: 500 !important;
    color: rgba(24, 18, 12, 0.86) !important;
  }
  .menu-drawer__menu--grid .menu-drawer__menu-item--child:hover,
  .menu-drawer__menu--grid .menu-drawer__menu-item--child:focus-visible {
    color: #18120C !important;
  }

  /* the crop fix: every source ratio renders as the same square */
  .menu-drawer__menu--grid .menu-drawer__link-image,
  .menu-drawer__menu--grid img {
    display: block !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    height: auto !important;
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1 !important;
    object-fit: cover !important;
    object-position: center !important;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0 !important;
    border-radius: 2px !important;
    background-color: #F0EBE3 !important;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(24, 18, 12, 0.10) !important;
  }

  /* -- dividers: hairline, warm, not full black -- */
  .menu-drawer__list-item--divider {
    border-color: rgba(24, 18, 12, 0.12) !important;
  }

  /* -- close button: real 44px tap target, aligned to the type column -- */
  .menu-drawer__close-button {
    min-width: 44px !important;
    min-height: 44px !important;
    display: inline-flex !important;
    align-items: center !important;
    justify-content: flex-start !important;
  }

  /* -- motion: slower, softer open than the theme's utilitarian .2s -- */
  .menu-drawer {
    transition:
      transform 0.42s cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.08, 0.24, 1),
      visibility 0.42s cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.08, 0.24, 1),
      opacity 0.42s cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.08, 0.24, 1) !important;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .menu-drawer {
      transition: none !important;
    }
  }

  /* -- full-screen panel on phones -- */
  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    .menu-drawer {
      inset: 0 !important;
      width: 100vw !important;
      max-width: 100vw !important;
      height: 100vh !important;
      max-height: 100vh !important;
      overflow-y: auto !important;
      overscroll-behavior: contain !important;
      -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch !important;
    }
    /* grow to fill a short menu, natural height for a tall one.
       NEVER a percentage min-height here - see BUGFIX note above. */
    .menu-drawer__navigation {
      flex: 1 0 auto !important;
      min-height: 0 !important;
    }
  }

  @supports (height: 100dvh) {
    @media (max-width: 749px) {
      .menu-drawer {
        height: 100dvh !important;
        max-height: 100dvh !important;
      }
    }
  }

  /* -- ACCORDION: collapsed by default, expand on tap --
     Everything here is gated on `html.ob-acc-js`, which the script adds only
     when it runs AND the browser supports :has(). Without that class the menu
     renders fully expanded, exactly as before, with every link working. */
  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    html.ob-acc-js .menu-drawer__navigation li:has(> ul):not([data-ob-acc='open']) > ul {
      display: none !important;
    }
    html.ob-acc-js .menu-drawer__navigation li:has(> ul) > a.menu-drawer__menu-item--mainlist {
      display: flex !important;
      align-items: center !important;
      justify-content: space-between !important;
      gap: 12px !important;
      width: 100% !important;
    }
    /* caret drawn with ::after rather than an injected element, so the theme's
       DOM morphing cannot strip it */
    html.ob-acc-js .menu-drawer__navigation li:has(> ul) > a.menu-drawer__menu-item--mainlist::after {
      content: '';
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      width: 8px;
      height: 8px;
      margin-inline-end: 4px;
      border-right: 1.5px solid currentColor;
      border-bottom: 1.5px solid currentColor;
      transform: rotate(-45deg);
      transform-origin: center;
      opacity: 0.5;
      transition: transform 0.25s cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.08, 0.24, 1);
    }
    html.ob-acc-js .menu-drawer__navigation li[data-ob-acc='open'] > a.menu-drawer__menu-item--mainlist::after {
      transform: rotate(45deg);
      opacity: 0.8;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html.ob-acc-js .menu-drawer__navigation li:has(> ul) > a.menu-drawer__menu-item--mainlist::after {
        transition: none;
      }
    }
    /* "View all" spans the grid so it doesn't sit in a half-width image slot */
    .ob-acc-viewall {
      grid-column: 1 / -1 !important;
      margin-block-start: 2px !important;
    }
    .ob-acc-viewall > a {
      text-decoration: underline !important;
      text-underline-offset: 3px !important;
      min-height: 40px !important;
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<script>
  (function () {
    /* The theme re-renders / morphs the drawer markup after DOMContentLoaded
       (note `data-skip-node-update` on the details container), which strips
       attributes and injected elements set at init time. VERIFIED: an earlier
       revision wired each row directly and every attribute was gone by the
       time the drawer was opened. So this version keeps NO persistent state in
       the drawer: the gate lives on <html>, the collapsed state and caret come
       from CSS, and the toggle is delegated on document. Nothing here needs to
       survive a re-render. */
    var MQ = window.matchMedia('(max-width: 749px)');

    /* Bail out entirely where :has() is unsupported, otherwise we would
       preventDefault on rows that CSS cannot expand, stranding the submenus. */
    if (!(window.CSS && CSS.supports && CSS.supports('selector(li:has(> ul))'))) return;

    document.documentElement.classList.add('ob-acc-js');

    function subOf(li) {
      for (var i = 0; i < li.children.length; i++) {
        if (li.children[i].tagName === 'UL') return li.children[i];
      }
      return null;
    }

    function linkOf(li) {
      for (var i = 0; i < li.children.length; i++) {
        if (li.children[i].tagName === 'A') return li.children[i];
      }
      return null;
    }

    /* Parent rows are real links. "About us" and "Bespoke" repeat themselves as
       their own first child so they lose nothing, but "Collections" does not -
       give it a "View all" so /collections stays reachable. Idempotent, and run
       on expand rather than at init so a re-render cannot lose it. */
    function ensureViewAll(a, sub) {
      var href = a.getAttribute('href');
      if (!href || href === '#' || sub.querySelector('.ob-acc-viewall')) return;
      var links = sub.querySelectorAll('a');
      for (var i = 0; i < links.length; i++) {
        if (links[i].getAttribute('href') === href) return;
      }
      var li = document.createElement('li');
      li.className = 'menu-drawer__list-item ob-acc-viewall';
      var link = document.createElement('a');
      link.className = 'menu-drawer__menu-item menu-drawer__menu-item--child';
      link.setAttribute('href', href);
      link.textContent = 'View all';
      li.appendChild(link);
      sub.appendChild(li);
    }

    document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      if (!MQ.matches) return; // desktop: ordinary links
      if (!e.target || !e.target.closest) return;

      var a = e.target.closest('a.menu-drawer__menu-item--mainlist');
      if (!a) return;

      var li = a.parentElement;
      if (!li || li.tagName !== 'LI') return;

      var sub = subOf(li);
      if (!sub) return; // leaf row: let it navigate

      e.preventDefault();

      var isOpen = li.getAttribute('data-ob-acc') === 'open';
      var topUl = li.parentElement;

      // single-open: collapse the others
      if (topUl) {
        for (var i = 0; i < topUl.children.length; i++) {
          var sib = topUl.children[i];
          if (sib === li) continue;
          sib.removeAttribute('data-ob-acc');
          var sa = linkOf(sib);
          if (sa) sa.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
        }
      }

      if (isOpen) {
        li.removeAttribute('data-ob-acc');
        a.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
      } else {
        li.setAttribute('data-ob-acc', 'open');
        a.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
        ensureViewAll(a, sub);
      }
    }, true); // capture, so this runs before the theme's own link handling
  })();
</script>
